---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: The end-to-end tests side by side
  accDescr: Once the job changes finds something to test, nine test jobs start at the same time. Three run the scenario, for Board Manager 1, Board Manager 2 and Home Assistant 2026.8.0. Six run the browser test, three for the current and three for the oldest supported Home Assistant, so all four shards of a version run at once, each on a demo instance of its own. The first runner of a version runs two workers, the cards, games and forms beside the steady heights; the second runs the tablet, every screen size, Firefox and the dartboard without Autodarts; the third runs the touch screens, Safari and accessibility alone, so that Safari's WebKit shares its CPU with no other browser. The required check e2e waits for all of them.

  CHANGES{{"changes: does the pull request<br/>change what the tests use?"}}
  CHANGES --> SCENARIO
  CHANGES --> CURRENT
  CHANGES --> OLDEST

  subgraph SCENARIO["scenario (run.sh)"]
    direction LR
    S1["Board Manager 1"] ~~~ S2["Board Manager 2"] ~~~ S3["Home Assistant<br/>2026.8.0"]
  end

  subgraph CURRENT["browser, current"]
    direction LR
    C1["runner 1, two workers<br/>shard 1/4: cards, games, forms<br/>shard 2/4: steady heights"]
    C2["runner 2<br/>shard 3/4: tablet,<br/>every screen size,<br/>Firefox, dartboard<br/>without Autodarts"]
    C3["runner 3<br/>shard 4/4: touch screens,<br/>Safari, accessibility"]
  end

  subgraph OLDEST["browser, 2026.8.0"]
    direction LR
    O1["runner 1<br/>shards 1/4 and 2/4"]
    O2["runner 2<br/>shard 3/4"]
    O3["runner 3<br/>shard 4/4"]
  end

  SCENARIO --> GATE["Required check e2e:<br/>passes when every job passed"]
  CURRENT --> GATE
  OLDEST --> GATE

  classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
  classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  class CHANGES bot
  class S1,S2,S3,C1,C2,C3,O1,O2,O3 bot
  class GATE done
